{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4gbaepnbkjwez4ziehzfae7khri3mmjf2nax3quwgrncp5sznoeq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumerated\nThe C library is small: `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` globs only `src/lib.c` (176 lines) with public header `include/lib.h`. Building the C `.so` and running `nm -D` gave **7 exported symbols** — all non-`static` functions in `lib.c`. There are no namespace-renaming macros in the header.\n\n| C symbol | Signature |\n|---|---|\n| `add_node` | `int(int, int, const char*, double)` |\n| `find_node_by_id` | `Node*(int)` |\n| `get_children_count` | `int(int)` |\n| `calculate_subtree_sum` | `double(int)` |\n| `process_string` | `int(char*)` |\n| `safe_double_to_int` | `int(double)` |\n| `maxnmin` | `int(int,int,int,int)` (the only header-declared one) |\n\n## Symbol-diff gate: EMPTY\n`comm -23` of the C export list vs. the Rust export list produced no output — Rust `liblib.so` exports all 7 names, no extras.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved\n- **`Node` layout**: `#[repr(C)]`, verified against C `sizeof`/`offsetof` (80 bytes; offsets 0, 4, 8, 64, 72) — matters because `find_node_by_id` hands out a raw pointer into static storage.\n- **Shared mutable statics**: `NODE_STORAGE`/`NODE_COUNT` are process-global, so state persists across calls exactly as in C (including `maxnmin` resetting `node_count = 0` without clearing the array).\n- **`strncpy` semantics**: copies ≤49 bytes, stops at NUL, zero-pads the rest, then forces `name[49] = 0`.\n- **Signed `char`**: `process_string` sign-extends bytes ≥ 0x80 (`*p as c_int`), reproducing negative contributions.\n- **`safe_double_to_int` check order kept**: `> INT_MAX` → `< INT_MIN` → NaN → truncate. The NaN test is *after* the range tests (as in C, where NaN comparisons are false), so NaN still returns 0. Range is pre-checked, so Rust's saturating `as i32` matches C truncation.\n- **Bugs